# The cargo tests that fail today on the C++ kernel (SOLIDCRAFT_KERNEL=smlib), one a line: `<test> <why it fails today>`, with the issue that
# tracks it when there is one. Sorted. `<test>` is nextest's `<binary id>::<test name>`, as the
# junit report names it. CI's test jobs (`cargo xtask known-failing`) fail on a test that fails
# and is not listed here, and on a listed test that passes: a fix removes its line in the same
# pull request. The tests stay un-ignored, so every run shows whether they still fail.
# Refresh (after an SMLib pin bump): download the junit artifacts of develop's latest CI run, one
# directory each (`gh run download <run> -R tangency-labs/solidcraft -n <artifact> -D <dir>/<artifact>`
# for junit and junit-gpu-1..4), run `cargo xtask known-failing --junit <dir>`, then drop each
# FIXED line and add each REGRESSION line with its cause, from the test's failure message.
# Baseline: develop 38fd4a4f6 (CI run 41157648345, x86_64 Linux), after the SMLib eaa998a pin; SMLib lines as of f916a8d (smlib 5862ee223).
solidcraft-cli::action_matrix::action_matrix_sample 2 baseline actions fail on SMLib: 2 shells (Bad Loop Orient on issue-616-lid-ribs; status 1001 on filleted-shelled-box, shelled again open at an inner wall)
solidcraft-cli::naming_corpus::corpus_designs_name_alike_every_build_and_fail_where_a_reference_is_gone oracle/83-boundary-loop-thicken does not load: step 8, SMLib thicken status 1001
solidcraft-engine::cmd::file::tests::each_format_has_an_export_command_of_its_own SMLib meshes a box's planar faces into 124 triangles, not 12 (the STL is 6284 bytes, the test counts 84 + 50 x 12)
solidcraft-engine::cmd::sketch_project::tests::intersection_curve_of_picked_faces_spans_the_whole_surface its premise fails on SMLib: the fit-point spline wall's 3 span faces are not one surface patch in SMLib's mesh (surface_patch gives 1 face, the test wants 3: truck's mesh hides those seams); the patch is taken through meeting_edges either way
solidcraft-engine::hole_face_tests::a_hole_wider_than_the_part_says_it_removes_all_of_it a 40 mm hole at (10, 10) touches the plate's edge y = 30 at one point; SMLib parts the plate there into 2 bodies, the test wants truck's 1
solidcraft-engine::measure_centre_tests::a_fillet_round_a_boss_reports_its_radius SMLib's round at the foot of a boss is not an analytic torus of minor radius 3, so no face of the body is (the test finds none to measure)
solidcraft-engine::tests::fillet_fit_taper_closes_to_a_point SMLib fillet status 1001 on the taper fit (radius 16 closing to 0)
solidcraft-engine::tests::mirror_placed::dragging_a_mirrored_part_meshes_its_copies_once a copy of a copy drawn from its first copy's triangles (#10101) is triangulated differently from SMLib's fresh mesh of it (one vertex more), where truck's meshes are the same under a rigid move
solidcraft-engine::tests::shell_tangent_chain_that_opens_every_face_explains_how_to_keep_walls SMLib shell status 1034 on a box with all 12 edges rounded (Ball corners since 5e8c9c1), opened at one face (tangency-labs/smlib#102)
solidcraft-kernel::blend::corner_tests::a_round_ending_in_an_earlier_round_matches_both_together SMLib fillet status 1001 on the round that ends in the earlier one
solidcraft-kernel::blend::corner_tests::corner_blends_hold_at_any_scale at 0.01x a picked edge runs on tangentially into an unblended edge and SMLib's result is not a closed solid (the smooth-vertex End, tangency-labs/smlib#81)
solidcraft-kernel::blend_corner::tests::issue2422_vertical_after_separate_bottom_rounds SMLib's check refuses the fillet: edge and vertex tolerance 0.97 against the body's 0.01 (#2422)
solidcraft-kernel::corner_g2::tests::a_long_setback_keeps_the_g2_patch_inside_the_box at set backs 11 to 15 the G2 corner patch bulges 2.6e-6 to 1.33e-3 past the box (the explicit corner is in progress)
solidcraft-kernel::corner_g2::tests::the_box_corner_g2_patch_is_a_closed_solid_curvature_continuous_to_its_neighbours the fitted G2 corner patch bulges 1.7e-5 past the box, which SMLib's exact tight box now sees (the explicit G2 corner builds it inside)
solidcraft-kernel::tests::fillet_tabbed_plate_outer_loop_and_partial_selection_after_hole the partial selection runs on tangentially into an unblended edge and SMLib's result is not a closed solid (the smooth-vertex End, tangency-labs/smlib#81)
